WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Tired of searching for subtitles?
Ray generates them instantly: getray.app

2
00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:32.991
Now. this is a musket.

3
00:00:33.492 --> 00:00:35.327
It's a gun. a weapon.

4
00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:36.829
-Gun.
-Gun.

5
00:00:36.912 --> 00:00:38.289
-Weapon.
-Weapon.

6
00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:40.249
-Weapon. That's right. Yeah.
-Weapon.

7
00:00:40.332 --> 00:00:43.168
Ball. Wad. Powder.

8
00:00:43.669 --> 00:00:45.588
-[imitates explosion] Yeah?
-[imitates explosion] Yeah.

9
00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:47.089
-[mumbles] Mouth?
-Mouth?

10
00:00:47.172 --> 00:00:49.008
-[speaks Hawaiian]
-There was a cape? The red?

11
00:00:49.091 --> 00:00:52.261
Red mouth.

12
00:00:52.344 --> 00:00:55.430
-Weapon.
-Red-mouthed weapon. That's right.

13
00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:30.800
Lion.

14
00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:32.593
[children] Lion.

15
00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:34.887
[John roars]

16
00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:37.139
[children roar in distance]

17
00:01:52.696 --> 00:01:53.697
[sighs]

18
00:02:19.598 --> 00:02:23.060
Barrel. Butt. Trigger.

19
00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:25.854
Cock. Flint.

20
00:02:26.522 --> 00:02:27.773
Frizzen.

21
00:02:27.856 --> 00:02:29.150
Now you're learning.

22
00:02:29.233 --> 00:02:30.567
That's good.

23
00:03:03.392 --> 00:03:04.393
[hammer cocks]

24
00:05:10.519 --> 00:05:13.063
[in Hawaiian] I thought you
would be back in Maui by now.

25
00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:19.736
I did not think I would have
to come to Oʻahu for you.

26
00:05:21.238 --> 00:05:22.823
[grunts]

27
00:05:24.992 --> 00:05:30.080
Oʻahu has not fallen as
easily as we thought.

28
00:05:33.292 --> 00:05:35.419
And you did not come to Oʻahu.

29
00:05:36.879 --> 00:05:38.088
I summoned you.

30
00:05:39.715 --> 00:05:40.883
You are my advisor.

31
00:05:47.764 --> 00:05:51.018
The Maui Chiefs are eager
for further conquest.

32
00:05:52.519 --> 00:05:55.522
They are hopeful to see
the Prophecy fulfilled.

33
00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:01.320
Let us hope we can
be worthy of it.

34
00:06:07.743 --> 00:06:08.744
My Prince.

35
00:06:10.621 --> 00:06:13.081
Your father is waiting for
you with his war party.

36
00:06:14.499 --> 00:06:15.501
What war party?

37
00:06:20.714 --> 00:06:22.090
We can't hold much longer.

38
00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.010
There are only a few
strongholds left.

39
00:06:26.929 --> 00:06:30.265
Kahekili acts on the
visions his god shows him.

40
00:06:32.017 --> 00:06:33.185
If we kill Kahekili.

41
00:06:34.686 --> 00:06:35.729
the vision dies with him.

42
00:06:36.855 --> 00:06:37.856
How?

43
00:06:40.442 --> 00:06:44.613
Our spies have poisoned the
food of the King's Council.

44
00:06:46.573 --> 00:06:47.824
They should return shortly.

45
00:06:48.325 --> 00:06:49.285
[bushes rustling]

46
00:06:49.368 --> 00:06:50.536
[warrior gasps]

47
00:07:10.055 --> 00:07:13.684
Your desperation has done this.

48
00:07:14.726 --> 00:07:15.727
old friend.

49
00:07:17.729 --> 00:07:19.815
You are lineage of
the great Kākuhihewa.

50
00:07:21.608 --> 00:07:25.529
Kneel before the Prophesied King

51
00:07:27.281 --> 00:07:31.619
and the last of Oʻahu's
Chiefs will follow.

52
00:07:31.702 --> 00:07:34.288
[breathes heavily]

53
00:07:44.339 --> 00:07:48.802
[captives whimpering. crying]

54
00:07:54.725 --> 00:07:55.726
Wait!

55
00:07:58.979 --> 00:08:02.232
Please. Not my family.

56
00:08:09.698 --> 00:08:11.241
I pledge to you my loyalty.

57
00:08:16.205 --> 00:08:17.206
my King.

58
00:08:18.582 --> 00:08:20.042
[scoffs. sighs]

59
00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:21.210
Loyalty?

60
00:08:21.752 --> 00:08:23.045
[scoffs]

61
00:08:26.673 --> 00:08:27.674
Loyalty.

62
00:08:28.926 --> 00:08:31.512
You chose poison for me.

63
00:08:33.096 --> 00:08:36.350
Now choose it for one of them.

64
00:08:38.477 --> 00:08:39.477
What?

65
00:08:44.358 --> 00:08:46.443
[whimpers]

66
00:08:52.908 --> 00:08:53.909
Please.

67
00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:57.871
Not this.

68
00:08:58.872 --> 00:09:00.374
[Kahekili] Your bloodline

69
00:09:01.708 --> 00:09:05.796
is not worthy to serve in
the Kingdom of Thunder.

70
00:09:08.549 --> 00:09:09.467
Kill them all.

71
00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:10.843
[grunts]

72
00:09:12.636 --> 00:09:15.014
-[shouts in Hawaiian]
-[captive whimpering]

73
00:09:15.097 --> 00:09:17.724
[chief screams]

74
00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:24.773
[captive splutters. chokes]

75
00:09:31.446 --> 00:09:32.948
[children laughing]

76
00:10:30.088 --> 00:10:31.381
[grunts]

77
00:10:35.886 --> 00:10:36.887
[grunts]

78
00:10:46.021 --> 00:10:47.314
[grunting]

79
00:10:57.866 --> 00:10:59.368
[gasps. grunts]

80
00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.161
[gasps. grunts]

81
00:11:06.291 --> 00:11:07.292
[warrior] Where is he?

82
00:11:12.339 --> 00:11:13.340
He's on the shore.

83
00:11:14.007 --> 00:11:15.207
[warriors] There's Kamehameha!

84
00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:19.638
[warriors laughing]

85
00:11:28.856 --> 00:11:30.858
You've been spending
much of your time here.

86
00:11:32.317 --> 00:11:34.653
You missed another
council meeting.

87
00:11:35.988 --> 00:11:38.323
This is no way to
lead your district.

88
00:11:38.824 --> 00:11:42.119
Here. with my warriors.
we yield results.

89
00:11:43.245 --> 00:11:45.831
At the council. we
yield more talk.

90
00:11:46.582 --> 00:11:47.833
There is news from Kaʻū.

91
00:11:49.001 --> 00:11:51.211
Your uncle's health grows worse.

92
00:11:53.088 --> 00:11:54.965
His time as king
is growing short.

93
00:11:57.759 --> 00:11:59.553
He has asked for you

94
00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:03.265
and your cousin.

95
00:12:56.443 --> 00:12:59.571
[king coughing]

96
00:13:07.287 --> 00:13:09.581
He is here. Father.

97
00:13:19.091 --> 00:13:20.801
Some have questioned

98
00:13:22.469 --> 00:13:24.721
why I keep the relics
of the Paleskin

99
00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:32.771
among the trophies
of conquered Chiefs.

100
00:13:34.565 --> 00:13:37.359
Captain Cook was a great Chief.

101
00:13:37.818 --> 00:13:40.946
He was an ignorant navigator.
surrounded by weak men.

102
00:13:42.656 --> 00:13:43.657
Nothing more.

103
00:13:46.326 --> 00:13:48.203
Stand Kamehameha.

104
00:13:49.997 --> 00:13:51.790
I am on the journey of death.

105
00:13:53.083 --> 00:13:55.127
My time is too short
for formalities.

106
00:13:56.295 --> 00:13:59.673
[coughing]

107
00:14:06.471 --> 00:14:08.348
King Kahekili grows stronger

108
00:14:09.391 --> 00:14:10.809
and will come to our shores.

109
00:14:12.436 --> 00:14:15.523
I fear the gods will deny me

110
00:14:15.606 --> 00:14:17.649
the greatest battle in the
history of our kingdoms.

111
00:14:19.067 --> 00:14:21.820
When I die.

112
00:14:22.988 --> 00:14:26.491
how will you protect Hawaiʻi?

113
00:14:27.993 --> 00:14:30.037
You hold the great God of War.

114
00:14:30.871 --> 00:14:32.331
No king has lost when...

115
00:14:32.414 --> 00:14:36.335
I will call Kahekili to the
blackened earth of Kaʻū.

116
00:14:37.336 --> 00:14:39.838
Here with the great God of War

117
00:14:40.631 --> 00:14:42.049
we will destroy him

118
00:14:42.132 --> 00:14:45.970
and silence the
thunder he worships.

119
00:14:46.053 --> 00:14:48.305
What say you. Kamehameha?

120
00:14:55.729 --> 00:14:57.529
Should the day come you
are no longer with us.

121
00:14:58.357 --> 00:14:59.733
Keōua will be king.

122
00:15:01.109 --> 00:15:02.694
I will follow where he leads.

123
00:15:03.612 --> 00:15:04.572
[grunts]

124
00:15:04.655 --> 00:15:07.908
Keōua is not king today.

125
00:15:08.492 --> 00:15:11.078
Speak your mind.

126
00:15:12.412 --> 00:15:17.417
How would you
protect our kingdom?

127
00:15:23.632 --> 00:15:25.551
I would increase
our food storage.

128
00:15:27.511 --> 00:15:29.096
In the battle of Kamokuhī.

129
00:15:30.138 --> 00:15:32.474
Hawaiʻi forces attacked
a post in Lānaʻi.

130
00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:34.935
With no food.

131
00:15:35.686 --> 00:15:38.105
the warriors were forced to
eat wild roots of kūpala.

132
00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:41.567
bringing a great
sickness of loose bowels.

133
00:15:42.359 --> 00:15:44.945
Hawaiʻi lost. not for
lack of warriors or spears

134
00:15:46.029 --> 00:15:48.907
but lack of food.

135
00:15:52.786 --> 00:15:54.580
Even if we began today

136
00:15:55.497 --> 00:15:57.875
it would take nine months
to have enough storage.

137
00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:01.128
I have already begun.

138
00:16:04.173 --> 00:16:07.843
We have storage huts near every
sacred site in Kohala's district.

139
00:16:12.014 --> 00:16:15.475
[coughing]

140
00:16:21.815 --> 00:16:23.650
I must rest.

141
00:16:37.414 --> 00:16:40.042
[John. in English] "...As they
that went before were affrighted."

142
00:16:41.293 --> 00:16:43.879
"Surely such are the
dwellings of the wicked."

143
00:16:45.923 --> 00:16:51.094
Uh. you said you would
tell me of your travels.

144
00:16:52.054 --> 00:16:53.096
Uh...

145
00:16:53.805 --> 00:16:56.350
A... Ala... Alaska?

146
00:16:56.433 --> 00:16:58.477
Yes. Alaska.

147
00:16:58.560 --> 00:16:59.770
Alaska.

148
00:17:00.395 --> 00:17:03.357
-Hmm.
-It is. um. real?

149
00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:05.150
Oh. it is real.

150
00:17:05.733 --> 00:17:09.029
A land of endless white snow.

151
00:17:09.863 --> 00:17:11.365
Frozen rain.

152
00:17:12.115 --> 00:17:13.116
[Moku] Kaʻahumanu.

153
00:17:21.083 --> 00:17:22.416
Stay. John.

154
00:17:23.126 --> 00:17:25.503
Our lesson for
today is not over.

155
00:17:28.841 --> 00:17:29.842
[in Hawaiian] It is time.

156
00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:34.930
[in English] I ask you to speak
English when John Young is here.

157
00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:36.932
[in Hawaiian] He
is neither warrior

158
00:17:37.891 --> 00:17:39.393
nor Chief

159
00:17:40.227 --> 00:17:41.645
and of no importance to me.

160
00:17:45.482 --> 00:17:48.360
[in English] Go
away. John Young.

161
00:18:00.038 --> 00:18:05.086
The High Priest said you marry
tonight under the moon of Māhealani.

162
00:18:05.169 --> 00:18:06.295
Not yet. please.

163
00:18:06.378 --> 00:18:09.840
[in English] We wait no more.

164
00:18:31.278 --> 00:18:34.364
[crew chattering]

165
00:18:35.449 --> 00:18:37.409
Take a generous pour. gentlemen.

166
00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:39.453
You've earned it.

167
00:18:43.207 --> 00:18:44.833
[friend] Some for Kaʻiana too.

168
00:18:45.334 --> 00:18:48.295
[crew mate] Still don't know why
Captain pulled him from the water.

169
00:18:49.463 --> 00:18:52.007
Sand lovin' devils would
never do that for us.

170
00:18:53.133 --> 00:18:54.510
He saved the captain.

171
00:18:57.596 --> 00:18:59.640
They killed John over there.

172
00:19:00.474 --> 00:19:03.644
Figured you'd care more about that
than your brown-bellied friend.

173
00:19:04.436 --> 00:19:07.356
If it were up to me. we'd go back
and take the island for ourselves.

174
00:19:07.439 --> 00:19:09.608
That's why ain't nothing
left up to you. Marley.

175
00:19:10.192 --> 00:19:13.403
[scoffs] You just an idiot
masquerading as a fool.

176
00:19:15.531 --> 00:19:19.117
Sailing open waters together
does not make us equal.

177
00:19:21.745 --> 00:19:24.039
Don't you forget that. boy.

178
00:19:42.182 --> 00:19:43.183
Your ration.

179
00:19:48.188 --> 00:19:52.067
If you don't want it. sell it
or trade with one of the men.

180
00:19:54.695 --> 00:19:57.823
They have nothing I want.

181
00:20:00.617 --> 00:20:03.662
You spend more time with these
guns than you do with the crew.

182
00:20:05.831 --> 00:20:06.999
I am not crew.

183
00:20:09.001 --> 00:20:11.420
I go home after trade.

184
00:20:12.171 --> 00:20:14.256
They need me there.

185
00:20:15.465 --> 00:20:16.466
Yes.

186
00:20:17.551 --> 00:20:19.011
Your Prophecy.

187
00:20:20.137 --> 00:20:21.305
[scoffs]

188
00:20:23.223 --> 00:20:27.311
As far as I've seen. Kaʻiana. men
of every color do unspeakable things

189
00:20:27.394 --> 00:20:30.189
for their gods and the
prophesies they believe in.

190
00:20:33.609 --> 00:20:34.860
I must go back.

191
00:20:36.528 --> 00:20:38.697
Uh-huh. I guess you'll
get your chance.

192
00:20:40.324 --> 00:20:43.327
Captain says we should reach
Zamboanga in the next day or so.

193
00:20:43.827 --> 00:20:45.204
You'll be heading
home after that.

194
00:20:48.498 --> 00:20:54.880
Is it true in Zamboanga
you can get anything?

195
00:20:56.673 --> 00:20:57.758
For a price.

196
00:21:03.013 --> 00:21:04.807
[panting]

197
00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:05.974
[in Hawaiian] Father!

198
00:21:18.362 --> 00:21:20.364
Why force me to marry now?

199
00:21:22.157 --> 00:21:24.034
King Kalaniʻōpuʻu is near death.

200
00:21:24.493 --> 00:21:26.787
Soon Kamehameha will
face more responsibility.

201
00:21:28.622 --> 00:21:30.457
You continue to
speak of politics

202
00:21:31.333 --> 00:21:34.711
but have yet to tell me
the real reason I am here.

203
00:21:35.462 --> 00:21:37.631
Kamehameha needs you.

204
00:21:38.048 --> 00:21:39.300
[sighs]

205
00:21:39.383 --> 00:21:41.218
I will be one of
many wives to come.

206
00:21:42.511 --> 00:21:43.671
What need does he have of me?

207
00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:48.440
I believe Kamehameha to
be the Prophesied One.

208
00:21:51.103 --> 00:21:52.104
How can this be?

209
00:21:52.771 --> 00:21:54.565
[sighs]

210
00:21:54.648 --> 00:21:57.067
I was Chief to
Kamehameha's father.

211
00:21:59.027 --> 00:22:01.238
I was there the
night he was born.

212
00:22:03.615 --> 00:22:07.119
It was the same night the prophetic
star burned across the sky.

213
00:22:09.788 --> 00:22:12.875
While everyone waited
for a king to rise.

214
00:22:16.295 --> 00:22:18.630
I saw a king born.

215
00:22:23.802 --> 00:22:24.970
[sighs]

216
00:22:25.053 --> 00:22:27.764
But he is hesitant
to accept who he is.

217
00:22:28.682 --> 00:22:29.683
But you

218
00:22:30.434 --> 00:22:33.520
trust in who you are.

219
00:22:35.480 --> 00:22:38.942
I need you to show him
how to do the same.

220
00:22:46.742 --> 00:22:48.327
[breathing heavily]

221
00:23:00.631 --> 00:23:01.757
[rock strikes tree]

222
00:23:09.515 --> 00:23:11.266
I have heard of your
abilities as a warrior.

223
00:23:18.440 --> 00:23:19.525
[in English] How are you?

224
00:23:24.071 --> 00:23:25.656
[in Hawaiian] I heard
you are to marry.

225
00:23:27.407 --> 00:23:28.742
[in English] How are you?

226
00:24:03.026 --> 00:24:04.111
[grunts]

227
00:24:04.194 --> 00:24:05.904
[bell ringing]

228
00:24:09.867 --> 00:24:12.077
[crew chattering]

229
00:24:19.376 --> 00:24:20.836
[captain] Listen up!

230
00:24:22.045 --> 00:24:24.548
To those of you leaving
us once we dock.

231
00:24:24.631 --> 00:24:27.510
I wish you well and
thank you for your work.

232
00:24:27.593 --> 00:24:31.263
For those staying on for the
expedition back to Alaska.

233
00:24:31.346 --> 00:24:33.724
remain close and conduct
yourselves appropriately.

234
00:24:33.807 --> 00:24:36.477
You know. don't get lost
at the bottom of a mug

235
00:24:36.560 --> 00:24:39.063
-or between the legs of some lass.
-[crew laughs]

236
00:24:39.146 --> 00:24:40.815
Prepare the cargo.

237
00:24:40.898 --> 00:24:43.692
The faster we unload. the
faster we all get paid.

238
00:25:13.847 --> 00:25:16.642
That's a King's ransom you're
holding in your hands. Kaʻiana.

239
00:25:17.351 --> 00:25:18.602
Men will trade for this?

240
00:25:18.685 --> 00:25:20.104
Oh. yes.

241
00:25:20.187 --> 00:25:22.606
And nothing better than
grog and a hot bath.

242
00:25:22.689 --> 00:25:24.107
[chuckles]

243
00:25:34.660 --> 00:25:36.411
[chattering]

244
00:26:22.040 --> 00:26:24.752
[friend] I know a place where
the grog and the food are good.

245
00:26:24.835 --> 00:26:25.919
but the women are ugly.

246
00:26:26.753 --> 00:26:28.130
That's just how I like it.

247
00:26:29.214 --> 00:26:30.215
Let's go.

248
00:27:00.621 --> 00:27:02.414
[metal banging]

249
00:27:13.342 --> 00:27:15.761
How may I be of service?

250
00:27:18.639 --> 00:27:21.725
-We trade.
-You would like to buy it?

251
00:27:23.018 --> 00:27:24.019
[Kaʻiana] Need more.

252
00:27:24.770 --> 00:27:26.104
[gunsmith] How many more?

253
00:27:27.356 --> 00:27:28.398
Many.

254
00:27:39.826 --> 00:27:40.869
[gunsmith laughs]

255
00:27:46.416 --> 00:27:49.503
You thought you could just go in there
and buy yourself an army's worth of guns?

256
00:27:49.586 --> 00:27:51.422
[chuckles] Come on.

257
00:27:51.505 --> 00:27:53.423
We can talk about
it over some food.

258
00:28:24.413 --> 00:28:25.664
Hey.

259
00:28:25.747 --> 00:28:28.542
Wait here. I may
be a minute or two.

260
00:28:36.383 --> 00:28:37.384
[drunk] You!

261
00:28:37.926 --> 00:28:39.178
You!

262
00:28:39.261 --> 00:28:40.846
What are you supposed to be?

263
00:28:42.848 --> 00:28:43.808
[burps]

264
00:28:43.891 --> 00:28:46.102
You look like a fucking peacock.

265
00:28:46.185 --> 00:28:49.063
-What is that... [gasps. groans]
-[growling]

266
00:28:49.146 --> 00:28:50.439
[in Hawaiian] You there.

267
00:28:54.443 --> 00:28:56.361
A Chief of Maui here?

268
00:28:59.948 --> 00:29:01.116
You're Hawaiian.

269
00:29:02.451 --> 00:29:03.452
Come.

270
00:29:05.621 --> 00:29:06.747
[groans]

271
00:29:06.830 --> 00:29:08.749
[scoffs. grunts]

272
00:29:23.222 --> 00:29:26.391
[in English] Welcome to the jewel
in Zamboanga's crown of shit.

273
00:29:27.601 --> 00:29:29.436
If you are looking for
trade. I am your woman.

274
00:29:30.145 --> 00:29:32.439
I've been everywhere. so
I can get you anything.

275
00:29:33.106 --> 00:29:34.191
-[hisses]
-[woman gasps]

276
00:29:34.983 --> 00:29:38.946
My name is Waineʻe. but the
Haole can never pronounce it.

277
00:29:39.530 --> 00:29:42.032
So they call me Vai.

278
00:29:42.616 --> 00:29:43.700
Who the hell are you?

279
00:29:45.911 --> 00:29:48.038
[in Hawaiian] I am
Kaʻiana. son of ʻAhuʻula.

280
00:29:51.542 --> 00:29:53.377
ʻAhuʻula?

281
00:29:54.586 --> 00:29:58.048
[in English] How does a chief of
Maui find himself in Zamboanga?

282
00:29:59.258 --> 00:30:00.551
[friend] We was lost.

283
00:30:01.176 --> 00:30:03.345
We got lucky in
finding them islands.

284
00:30:03.428 --> 00:30:04.972
Picked him up along the way.

285
00:30:07.558 --> 00:30:08.851
Your ship is still here?

286
00:30:09.560 --> 00:30:11.061
[friend] For a few more days.

287
00:30:11.144 --> 00:30:15.023
Captain has another expedition planned.
said he'd take Kaʻiana home after that.

288
00:30:18.360 --> 00:30:20.404
But first. we get
red-mouth weapon.

289
00:30:20.487 --> 00:30:22.823
I don't know how you're gonna
get enough guns for an army.

290
00:30:28.161 --> 00:30:29.329
Why do you need guns?

291
00:30:36.128 --> 00:30:39.882
[in Hawaiian] I made a
mistake. I must fix it.

292
00:30:41.341 --> 00:30:42.467
[in English] With guns?

293
00:30:43.594 --> 00:30:45.304
It must have been a big mistake.

294
00:30:54.104 --> 00:30:55.105
[in Spanish] Go!

295
00:30:58.817 --> 00:30:59.818
Go!

296
00:31:04.323 --> 00:31:05.365
Kaʻiana.

297
00:31:07.075 --> 00:31:08.869
[in English] Speak English here.

298
00:31:08.952 --> 00:31:12.497
And change into something that
does not turn too many heads.

299
00:31:16.251 --> 00:31:17.794
I can get your guns.

300
00:31:21.882 --> 00:31:24.259
[in Hawaiian] Why help me?

301
00:31:26.303 --> 00:31:29.056
[in English] Because you
are going to help me.

302
00:31:31.725 --> 00:31:32.726
[Kaʻiana] Mmm.

303
00:31:38.857 --> 00:31:42.402
We have just finished the longest
haul this ship has ever seen.

304
00:31:43.237 --> 00:31:44.405
Right.

305
00:31:44.488 --> 00:31:47.282
Now. I have no love for
these Spanish bastards.

306
00:31:47.950 --> 00:31:49.910
but they pay well... [laughs]

307
00:31:49.993 --> 00:31:54.748
...and they are hungry for
anything that I might bring 'em.

308
00:31:55.541 --> 00:31:59.670
But what kind of deal would I need
from the likes of. you know. you? Yeah?

309
00:32:01.380 --> 00:32:02.798
Kaʻiana needs guns.

310
00:32:03.465 --> 00:32:04.591
Guns?

311
00:32:07.052 --> 00:32:09.138
I couldn't get you
guns if I wanted to.

312
00:32:09.221 --> 00:32:11.515
It's too much trouble with
the officials. you know.

313
00:32:11.598 --> 00:32:13.642
I have friends who
work around them.

314
00:32:13.725 --> 00:32:14.893
Ah.

315
00:32:15.519 --> 00:32:17.521
So smugglers? Right.

316
00:32:18.272 --> 00:32:20.023
So you're looking for a loan.

317
00:32:21.233 --> 00:32:22.693
See...

318
00:32:24.736 --> 00:32:27.239
afraid that's not a business
I entertain. either.

319
00:32:29.074 --> 00:32:33.453
You will be repaid with a
business endeavor men kill for.

320
00:32:39.209 --> 00:32:40.211
[captain] Sandalwood?

321
00:32:40.294 --> 00:32:41.753
[speaks Hawaiian]

322
00:32:42.337 --> 00:32:43.798
[in English] It is so rare

323
00:32:43.881 --> 00:32:47.343
that a trader from Zamboanga can
sell it for five times its value

324
00:32:47.426 --> 00:32:49.428
in both China and Europe.

325
00:32:50.137 --> 00:32:52.431
And our islands have
mountains full of it.

326
00:32:53.682 --> 00:32:56.143
You want to start
a sandalwood trade?

327
00:32:56.226 --> 00:32:57.686
[Vai] We would be partners.

328
00:32:57.769 --> 00:33:00.564
It will make you richer than
you ever thought possible.

329
00:33:01.481 --> 00:33:05.068
[captain] Well. we would
only be one ship. you know.

330
00:33:05.777 --> 00:33:08.405
So how would we compete
against East India?

331
00:33:09.281 --> 00:33:11.825
They do not know where
our small islands lie.

332
00:33:12.492 --> 00:33:16.663
And you will have Kaʻiana to help convince
the chiefs of our home to allow it.

333
00:33:17.247 --> 00:33:18.707
You sell our home?

334
00:33:19.625 --> 00:33:23.420
[speaks Hawaiian]

335
00:33:24.129 --> 00:33:25.130
[in English] No.

336
00:33:25.714 --> 00:33:27.341
The trade would be ours.

337
00:33:27.424 --> 00:33:29.676
The money to benefit our people.

338
00:33:30.802 --> 00:33:32.763
It will work. Kaʻiana.

339
00:33:33.680 --> 00:33:35.807
I have thought about
this for many years.

340
00:33:39.561 --> 00:33:40.896
Yeah. it could work.

341
00:33:42.022 --> 00:33:45.234
You have been gone too long.

342
00:33:48.111 --> 00:33:51.240
[in Hawaiian] You see the
world like the Paleskin.

343
00:33:55.536 --> 00:33:57.829
You should too. Kaʻiana.

344
00:34:02.751 --> 00:34:03.794
[door closes]

345
00:34:07.214 --> 00:34:08.340
[grunts]

346
00:34:10.926 --> 00:34:13.721
[Vai. in English] It was
not always like this here.

347
00:34:13.804 --> 00:34:16.348
This was their home
before the Spanish came.

348
00:34:16.431 --> 00:34:18.100
They took everything.

349
00:34:18.725 --> 00:34:21.395
They will come to our islands.
Turn that into another Zamboanga.

350
00:34:21.478 --> 00:34:22.480
[scoffs]

351
00:34:22.563 --> 00:34:23.647
We will fight them.

352
00:34:23.730 --> 00:34:25.982
With what? Your spear?

353
00:34:26.065 --> 00:34:28.694
That is no match for their guns

354
00:34:28.777 --> 00:34:34.449
and the Pale-man's greed is stronger
than any god or prophesy you fight for.

355
00:34:36.326 --> 00:34:37.995
There has to be another way.

356
00:34:39.204 --> 00:34:45.377
It is only a matter of time before our
waters will be full of foreign ships.

357
00:34:46.085 --> 00:34:49.339
all of which to trade
or to take what we have.

358
00:34:50.424 --> 00:34:55.804
Sandalwood is money. and money
is all the Pale-man respect.

359
00:34:57.264 --> 00:34:59.683
Maybe all you respect. too.

360
00:35:01.602 --> 00:35:04.104
We can control the
future of our people.

361
00:35:05.272 --> 00:35:08.108
But we cannot do it
without you. Kaʻiana.

362
00:35:09.401 --> 00:35:13.322
You are the only chief who knows
what will come to our shores.

363
00:35:15.949 --> 00:35:19.828
Either we control the trade
or we lose everything.

364
00:35:24.291 --> 00:35:27.127
Get your guns and
let us return home.

365
00:35:38.013 --> 00:35:40.641
[person speaking Spanish]

366
00:35:40.724 --> 00:35:42.768
[captive grunting]

367
00:35:49.525 --> 00:35:51.245
[in English] Good
evening. Captain Metcalfe.

368
00:35:53.237 --> 00:35:54.572
[Marley] Captain Metcalfe.

369
00:35:54.655 --> 00:35:55.781
Do I know you?

370
00:35:56.406 --> 00:35:59.994
I'm Marley. a blacksmith
and armorer by trade.

371
00:36:00.077 --> 00:36:01.912
I have crew. Mr. Marley.

372
00:36:01.995 --> 00:36:04.373
I'm not looking
for a job. Captain.

373
00:36:04.456 --> 00:36:08.669
There's a cluster of unmapped
islands deep in the Pacific.

374
00:36:08.752 --> 00:36:11.505
Untouched by the hands
of Christian men.

375
00:36:12.381 --> 00:36:14.175
Whoever takes these islands

376
00:36:14.258 --> 00:36:18.595
can control the pathways of the
Pacific from Alaska to Canton.

377
00:36:19.388 --> 00:36:24.017
Why. we'd be the kings
of our own paradise.

378
00:36:25.561 --> 00:36:27.145
Why bring this to me?

379
00:36:28.021 --> 00:36:30.732
I've seen the Sand
Savage up close.

380
00:36:31.400 --> 00:36:35.195
They are a warrior people with
no fear of musket and cannon.

381
00:36:35.779 --> 00:36:36.864
as of yet.

382
00:36:37.614 --> 00:36:44.329
Few trade-captains would be willing
to do what must be done in order to...

383
00:36:44.913 --> 00:36:46.790
[sighs] ...tame them.

384
00:37:05.517 --> 00:37:06.518
[in Hawaiian] Father.

385
00:37:09.021 --> 00:37:10.022
So you know.

386
00:37:10.939 --> 00:37:14.776
your mother and I did not betroth
you without careful consideration.

387
00:37:17.154 --> 00:37:19.031
You have a duty to your Chief.

388
00:37:29.750 --> 00:37:34.171
You think that I would give my
only daughter away out of duty?

389
00:37:38.675 --> 00:37:39.676
[sighs]

390
00:37:40.177 --> 00:37:41.178
As king.

391
00:37:44.181 --> 00:37:47.893
Kamehameha will
face many unknowns.

392
00:37:48.936 --> 00:37:52.022
The gods have made it
clear to me. Kaʻahumanu.

393
00:37:54.399 --> 00:37:56.151
the person he needs is you.

394
00:38:01.990 --> 00:38:06.787
Then why have the gods
kept their secrets from me?

395
00:38:11.875 --> 00:38:15.838
As a Chief's wife. my first
duty is to bear him a son.

396
00:38:16.296 --> 00:38:17.881
an heir to help
spread his legacy.

397
00:38:26.390 --> 00:38:30.352
The Prophetess saw
nothing for me.

398
00:38:32.729 --> 00:38:37.401
She said the seed of
Kamehameha cannot live in me.

399
00:38:38.277 --> 00:38:39.278
What does that mean?

400
00:38:41.530 --> 00:38:43.991
It means I will never
bear him children.

401
00:38:49.621 --> 00:38:51.290
When he sees there
is no future with me.

402
00:38:51.373 --> 00:38:54.042
he will turn to a wife
that can carry his child.

403
00:38:58.380 --> 00:39:00.716
I am so sorry. Father.

404
00:39:02.092 --> 00:39:05.345
but I will never be
what you hoped for.

405
00:39:14.688 --> 00:39:18.025
Never tell him this.

406
00:39:30.913 --> 00:39:32.915
[chattering]

407
00:39:41.924 --> 00:39:44.801
[speaks indistinctly]

408
00:39:58.482 --> 00:39:59.566
Well. what's your name?

409
00:40:00.400 --> 00:40:01.401
Ah.

410
00:40:03.570 --> 00:40:05.906
Come on. You show me the way.

411
00:40:37.020 --> 00:40:38.480
[person singing in Hawaiian]

412
00:40:49.408 --> 00:40:51.410
[singing continues]

413
00:41:10.012 --> 00:41:11.013
[singing stops]

414
00:41:19.229 --> 00:41:24.610
Greetings to you. the
finest blossom of East Maui.

415
00:41:31.158 --> 00:41:35.037
[singing resumes]

416
00:41:55.057 --> 00:41:57.059
[singing continues]

417
00:42:14.201 --> 00:42:18.872
As his newest wife. you
will share his bed as we do.

418
00:42:19.957 --> 00:42:21.397
Your life will be
in service of his.

419
00:42:21.667 --> 00:42:23.794
Do not fight it. Kaʻahumanu.

420
00:42:25.420 --> 00:42:30.759
Your children will bring the
union of Hawaiʻi with Maui.

421
00:42:31.176 --> 00:42:32.553
It is a blessing.

422
00:42:32.928 --> 00:42:34.054
[in English] What is this?

423
00:42:34.137 --> 00:42:35.305
Hoʻomaukeiki.

424
00:42:35.931 --> 00:42:39.226
The gods ask Kaʻahumanu
to give Kamehameha a son.

425
00:42:42.479 --> 00:42:44.398
To the woman in
the rising flame.

426
00:42:45.148 --> 00:42:47.401
there was a seeking of
the lost. Now it is found.

427
00:42:48.735 --> 00:42:53.282
A mate is found. one to
share the chills of winter.

428
00:42:54.324 --> 00:42:55.367
The sky is changing.

429
00:42:56.952 --> 00:42:58.996
Hākoʻilani. the house
of respite is secured.

430
00:42:59.913 --> 00:43:02.332
Love has made a plea that
you two become united.

431
00:43:03.166 --> 00:43:05.502
Here is a perch. a
heavenly resting place.

432
00:43:06.753 --> 00:43:09.423
You two are now one.
The darkness withdraws.

433
00:43:10.174 --> 00:43:11.592
The east is beginning
to brighten.

434
00:43:12.634 --> 00:43:13.754
For the day is here at last!

435
00:43:18.015 --> 00:43:21.810
The night is kapu until the
light of the day arrives.

436
00:43:22.644 --> 00:43:23.645
You are wedded.

437
00:43:24.229 --> 00:43:25.230
free to each other.

438
00:43:27.149 --> 00:43:28.269
The prayer has taken flight.

439
00:43:30.152 --> 00:43:31.153
The day is here.

440
00:43:31.695 --> 00:43:32.696
The prayer is said.

441
00:43:33.238 --> 00:43:34.239
The kapu is freed.

442
00:45:01.493 --> 00:45:04.496
I pray the gods have
blessed us this night.

443
00:45:06.915 --> 00:45:08.417
Yes. my Chief.

444
00:46:14.399 --> 00:46:18.320
[Marley] You move real easy in the dark
with that nigger skin. don't ya. boy?

445
00:46:18.403 --> 00:46:20.072
What the hell are you
doing here. Marley?

446
00:46:20.614 --> 00:46:21.615
[chuckles]

447
00:46:21.698 --> 00:46:24.034
-I just... Captain asked me to...
-[gun cocks]

448
00:46:24.117 --> 00:46:25.994
Captain never told you nothing.

449
00:46:28.455 --> 00:46:29.373
Yeah.

450
00:46:29.456 --> 00:46:31.959
Well. why don't we wait for him to
come back and we'll see what he said.

451
00:46:32.042 --> 00:46:33.126
[gun cocks]

452
00:46:41.385 --> 00:46:42.427
[grunts]

453
00:46:45.347 --> 00:46:47.558
[grunting. groaning]

454
00:46:56.608 --> 00:46:58.527
He'd be worth more
alive than dead.

455
00:46:59.987 --> 00:47:01.697
[panting]

456
00:47:01.780 --> 00:47:03.156
[Marley] Did ya hear that?

457
00:47:04.741 --> 00:47:07.160
I'm gonna send you
back where you belong.

458
00:47:08.537 --> 00:47:11.540
[grunts. exclaims]

459
00:47:24.845 --> 00:47:26.514
No. No.

460
00:47:26.597 --> 00:47:29.433
No! No...

461
00:47:29.516 --> 00:47:30.934
[panting]

462
00:47:33.103 --> 00:47:34.104
[grunts]

463
00:47:39.026 --> 00:47:40.027
[grunts]

464
00:47:42.529 --> 00:47:43.739
Get out of here.

465
00:47:44.656 --> 00:47:45.949
[grunts]

465
00:47:46.305 --> 00:48:46.875
